 Saving TabId= 19  Internal table number=    4
  
  
         Example of the FEQXEXT command.  It permits optional                    
         variation of Manning's n in the vertical in each subsection.            
         In the example shown here subsections 1 and 2 have request              
         such variation.  The * in the column headed N0 selects                  
         the n value given for the subsection on the line labeled                
         with NSUB as the roughness to use at zero depth in the                  
         subsection.  Thus in subsection 1 the Manning's n is                    
         0.140 at zero depth and varies linearly with water                      
         depth until a depth is 1.0.  Above that level the                       
         n value is constant.  The choice of depth is given                      
         on the VARN line.  MAXY uses the maximum depth in the                   
         subsection as the variable to which variation of n is                   
         related.  Another options in HYDY, hydraulic depth in                   
         the subsection.   Comments for each boundary point                      
         can be given but they must be prefixed by a single                      
         quote.                                                                  
  
         Subsection 3 shows an example of having the n                           
         value on the boundary vary from one line segment                        
         to the next.  FEQXEXT computes a perimeter-weighted                     
         value of Manning's n in this case.  The * is needed                     
         to signal that the subsection number is to take                         
         the default value.  The default for a subsection number is              
         always the most recent subsection number encountered.                   
  
  
  
 FEQXEXT                                                                         

 Processing:TABID=   154 OUT22 OLDBETA

 Processing:STATION=     1.25

 Processing:VARN=MAXY

 Processing:NSUB    3      .140      .050      .140

