         Example of computing a table for use in the CHANRAT command.            
         This if for one of the over banks of a cross section.  Note that        
         the EXTEND option has been added to the list of options.                
         If this is not done,  the global EXTEND=NO option at the                
         start of the input would prevent this table from being                  
         computed.  Notice that one end of the cross section stops               
         at an elevation of zero.  If automatic extension of the ends            
         of cross sections is enabled, FEQUTL will extend the low                
         end of the cross section with a vertical frictionless wall              
         to enable computation of the table.  If automatic extension             
         is suppressed then FEQUTL will not extend the low end and               
         the table argument, depth, will be limited to the value                 
         defined by the end of the cross section with minimum elevation.         
  
         If automatic extension is used and if one side of the cross section     
         is lower than the other and if the water level in FEQ rises above       
         the low end then FEQ ISSUES NO WARNING.   Therefore automatic           
         extension should be used with care.                                     
  
