         CHANRAT- computes a channel rating for a short prismatic channel        
         assuming steady flow.  The bottom slope must always result in           
         subcritical flow.  Should super critical flow result, FEQUTL will       
         signal an error and go to the next command.  Note that                  
         bottom slopes less than or equal to zero compute more quickly.          
         Very small slopes greater than zero compute  slowly and                 
         computations may break down.  Thus the best choice if the slope         
         is small is to use zero.  The difference between a slope of             
         1 in 10,000 and 0 on the table is small.                                
  
         CHANRAT computes a 2-D table of either type 6 or 13.                    
         Tables of type 13 take less space and are easier to                     
         read.  The head is always measured from the high point of               
         the channel.  If BOTSLP > 0 then the datum for head is the              
         upstream end of the channel otherwise the datum for head is             
         the downstream end of the channel.                                      
  
  
  
