         The weir is trapezoidal and has a thickness of                          
         6 inches.                                                               
  
  
         The weir crest in this case is trapezoidal with side slopes of          
         1:1.  Four points would define the crest but I have placed extra        
         points on the sloping part of the crest to improve the                  
         numerical integration accuracy.  EMBANKQ approximates the               
         integral of a unit length weir equation using Simpson's rule            
         on each interval defined by the points along the crest.                 
  
         FEQUTL also assumes that the width to use for the weir is               
         the width in the opening at the upstream piezometric surface.           
         This width is wider than the actual wetted width.  However,             
         limited testing using observations reported for triangular weirs        
         supports this assumption.                                               
  
