 *     Test of channel with symmetrical triangular channel with
 *     large values of constant and linearly varying sinuousity.
 *     Note that the value of MA is always 1.0 in a symmetrical
 *     channel with the distace axis on the line of symmetry.
 *     MQ is not 1.0 because our assumption that the decline in
 *     the total energy line is constant between two sections
 *     entails that the friction slope is no longer constant.
 *     This causes an asymmetry in the distribution
 *     of flow with more flow taking the shorter path.  Thus
 *     MQ will be slightly less than 1.0 in a sinuous symmetrical
 *     channel.
  
 CHANNEL                                                                         
 SINDEF=LINEAR                                                                   
 HEAD     LFB    AXIS     RFB                                                    
  
 STAT   0.000   0.000   0.000                                                    
 OFFS    0.00   10.00   20.00                                                    
  
 STAT   1.500   1.000   0.500                                                    
 OFFS    0.00   10.00   20.00                                                    
  
 STAT   3.000   2.000   1.000                                                    
 OFFS    0.00   10.00   20.00                                                    
  
 END                                                                             

